    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19344" root="سدف" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَدَفٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُدْفَةٌ</span>, in three places. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also The
<i>night.</i> (S, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  And The <i>daybreak,</i> or <i>dawn:</i>
(AA, S, K:) and the <i>advent thereof:</i> (Fr, S, K:)
and the <i>whiteness of day.</i> (TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>A ewe:</i>
(Ibn-'Abbád, K:) or <i>such as has a blackness like
that of night.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَدَفْ سَدَفْ</span> is <i>A
call to the ewe to be milked.</i> (K.)

